-- title:
--   Information filtration of the lookahead observations
-- statement:
--   The filtration generated by the process $Z^1,Z^2,\dots$ of the lookahead: at time $\tau$ it contains the information in the first $\tau$ lookahead observations of arm $i$. The stopping times $T_i$ in the cPDE index are stopping times of this filtration.
--
--   **Formalization Note** It is the natural filtration of $Z$, not the coordinate filtration of the canonical space, which would reveal $\omega_0$ (the true $\theta_i$) at time $0$.
-- source:
--   Chick, Gans & Yapar, Bayesian Sequential Learning for Clinical Trials of Multiple Correlated Medical Interventions, SSRN preprint 3184758 (version of August 31, 2020), p. 10 (§3.2, policies in Π_i)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CPDETrial_zProc
open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology
open scoped NNReal ENNReal

namespace CPDETrial

/-- **The information filtration of the lookahead observations.**
Chick, Gans & Yapar, *Bayesian Sequential Learning for Clinical Trials of Multiple Correlated
Medical Interventions*, SSRN preprint 3184758 (version of August 31, 2020), §3.2, p. 10: the policies `π_i ∈ Π_i` "sample only from arm `i`" and decide when to stop
from what they have observed; their stopping times `T_i` are stopping times of the observations.

`zFilt l s` is the natural filtration of the process `τ ↦ zProc l s τ`: at time `τ` it holds the
information in `Z^1, …, Z^τ`, equivalently in the first `τ` lookahead observations (for `s > 0`,
`Z^τ` is an invertible affine function of the partial sum of the observations).

**Formalization Note.** This is deliberately **not** the coordinate filtration of `ℕ → ℝ`: that
one would reveal `ω 0 = (θ_i − µ_i)/√Σ_ii` at time `0` and turn the index into a perfect
information value. -/
noncomputable def zFilt (l : ℝ≥0) (s : ℝ) : Filtration ℕ (MeasurableSpace.pi : MeasurableSpace (ℕ → ℝ)) :=
  Filtration.natural (fun τ => zProc l s τ) (fun τ => by
    apply Measurable.stronglyMeasurable
    unfold zProc
    fun_prop)

end CPDETrial


